 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, multiplexer and internal 2.5 V reference (REFOUT never driven): every conversion returns the 0 V differential code 000h",
  "SERIAL DATA B (converter B, Mode I/III) is never driven; SERIAL DATA A shifts Mode I's 16-cell word (channel flag = A0 level, A/B flag 0, D11..D0, 0, 0). Mode II/IV (M1 = 1: A then B on SERIAL DATA A, 32 clocks, the second CONVST ignored) and Mode III/IV automatic channel sequencing (M0 = 1) are not modeled; M0/M1 are stored only",
  "the serial frame is delimited by RD (the model's chip select: the frame starts when the active-high RD sync pulse returns low, data shift on CLOCK rising edges and are valid on falling edges); the CS pin's tri-state gating of the serial outputs is not modeled, so keep CS low",
  "the channel flag is the A0 level at the frame start, not the address latched on CLOCK cycle 1/2 for the next conversion",
  "the conversion is clocked by the external CLOCK (16 cycles after the CONVST-to-CLOCK synchronisation of Figure 8); the model uses tCONV 1.75 us at tCKP = 125 ns; BUSY returning low after the third LSB is approximated by the end of tCONV",
  "pin names: the minus sign of CH xx- is written '-'"
 ],
